      "title": "Tree Profile",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "height, width = map(int, input().split())\nexpected_width = 1\nvalid = True\nhas_crown = False\nhas_trunk = False\nwidths = []\n\nfor _ in range(height):\n    row = input()\n    row_width = row.count(\"@\") + row.count(\"#\")\n    if row_width == 0:\n        continue\n    if \"#\" in row:\n        has_trunk = True\n        expected_width = 1\n    if row_width != expected_width:\n        valid = False\n    widths.append(row_width)\n    if \"@\" in row:\n        has_crown = True\n        expected_width += 2\n\nif valid and has_crown and has_trunk:\n    print(*widths)\nelse:\n    print(\"INVALID\")\n",
      "statement": "In a tree, {{@}} forms the crown and {{#}} forms the trunk. Ignore all other characters.\n\n<<Valid tree>>\n• A valid tree has at least one crown row and at least one trunk row.\n• The crown starts with a width of {{1}}. Each subsequent crown row must be {{2}} characters wider than the previous crown row. Thus, the crown widths start with {{1}}, {{3}}, {{5}}, …. The crown may stop after any number of rows.\n• Every trunk row must have width {{1}}.\n\nIf the given picture contains a valid tree, print all tree row widths from top to bottom, separated by spaces. Otherwise, print {{INVALID}}.\n\n<<The following are guaranteed, and checking them is not required in your code:>>\nFor every row containing {{@}} or {{#}}:\n• A row contains either {{@}} or {{#}}, never both.\n• All {{@}} and {{#}} characters form one contiguous block, both horizontally and vertically.\n• The block is horizontally centered within the picture.\n• All crown rows appear above all trunk rows.",
