    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">In a tree, <const>@</const> forms the crown and <const>#</const> forms the trunk. Ignore all other characters.<br><br><strong>Valid tree</strong><br>&bull; A valid tree has at least one crown row and at least one trunk row.<br>&bull; The crown starts with a width of <const>1</const>. Each subsequent crown row must be <const>2</const> characters wider than the previous crown row. Thus, the crown widths start with <const>1</const>, <const>3</const>, <const>5</const>, &hellip;. The crown may stop after any number of rows.<br>&bull; Every trunk row must have width <const>1</const>.<br><br>If the given picture contains a valid tree, print all tree row widths from top to bottom, separated by spaces. Otherwise, print <const>INVALID</const>.<br><br><strong>The following are guaranteed, and checking them is not required in your code:</strong><br>For every row containing <const>@</const> or <const>#</const>:<br>&bull; A row contains either <const>@</const> or <const>#</const>, never both.<br>&bull; All <const>@</const> and <const>#</const> characters form one contiguous block, both horizontally and vertically.<br>&bull; The block is horizontally centered within the picture.<br>&bull; All crown rows appear above all trunk rows.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> Two integers <var>h</var> and <var>w</var>, the picture's height and odd width.<br><strong>Next <var>h</var> lines:</strong> A string <var>row</var> of exactly <var>w</var> characters.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>One line:</strong> The crown and trunk row widths, separated by spaces, or <const>INVALID</const>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>h</var>, <var>w</var> &le; 31<br><var>w</var> is odd.<br>Each <var>row</var> contains exactly <var>w</var> printable ASCII characters, possibly including spaces.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">7 11\n*.......*..\n..*........\n.....@.....\n....@@@....\n...@@@@@...\n.....#.....\nv_v_v_v_v_v</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1 3 5 1</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
